{
  "algorithm": {
    "id": "config-v2-cross-field",
    "specification": "architecture/config/config.schema.yaml",
    "summary": "The five endpoint cross-field rules stated in the schema: unique endpoint IDs; a set default naming an ENABLED endpoint; static-subset peers being a subset of trust.allowed_peers; endpoint policy narrowing rather than widening profile trust (ADR-0012); and enabled advertised entries fitting directory.max_advertised. Verdict set.",
    "why_not_json_schema": "Each rule is a relationship BETWEEN fields. JSON Schema constrains shape, not agreement between two branches of a document, which is exactly the gap these vectors cover beside contracts/schemas/.",
    "wire_shape": "Endpoint policies use the shape frozen by endpoints/endpoint-config.schema.json: the bare string \"inherit_profile_trust\", or {\"static_subset\": [...]}. An earlier revision of this file used a Serde-tagged {\"policy\": ...} form that the schema never accepted — corrected as a defect, not a protocol change, since no shape ever validated both ways."
  },
